      "dom_id": "step-q62202",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$(2+3)-{2}^{2}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We use PEMDAS. We start with the **P**arentheses:\n\n$$\n{{(2+3)}_{⏟}}_{5}-{2}^{2}=5-{2}^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we find the **E**xponents:\n\n$$\n5\\,-\\overset{4}{\\overset{⏞}{{2}^{2}}}=5\\,-4\n$$\n\nFinally, we perform the **S**ubtraction:\n\n$$\n5-4=1\n$$",
