      "problem": "$(6-2)+{2}^{3}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We use PEMDAS. We start with the **P**arentheses:\n\n$$\n{{(6-2)}_{⏟}}_{4}+{2}^{3}=4+{2}^{3}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we find the **E**xponents:\n\n$$\n4\\,+\\overset{8}{\\overset{⏞}{{2}^{3}}}=4+8\n$$\n\nFinally, we perform the **A**ddition:\n\n$$\n4+8=12\n$$",
