      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$5\\times (1+{2}^{3})=$",
      "worked_solution": "According to PEMDAS, we should first calculate the expression inside the **P**arentheses: $(1+{2}^{3}).$\n\n To evaluate $(1+{2}^{3})$ we should also apply PEMDAS. We start with the **E**xponents:\n\n$$\n1\\,+\\overset{8}{\\overset{⏞}{{2}^{3}}}=1+8\n$$\n\nThen, we perform the **A**ddition:\n\n$$\n1+8=9\n$$\n\nSo we have:\n\n$$\n5\\times {{(1+{2}^{3})}_{⏟}}_{9}=5\\times 9\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we perform the **M**ultiplication:\n\n$$\n5\\times 9=45\n$$",
